In this case, since the police did not inform the family at all—despite the arrest occurring on 10 May 2026 and the brother being found only the next afternoon—their failure to comply with these requirements constitutes a violation of the Appellate Division’s directive. The police were legally obligated to notify the family within twelve hours, which they failed to do.

Therefore, under the guidelines established in *Bangladesh & ors Vs. BLAST & ors*, the police should have immediately informed a relative (or a friend if no relative was available) about the arrest, including the time and place of detention, and recorded this information in their diary. Their failure to do so is a breach of fundamental procedural safeguards for arrested persons.
